From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shahed <jamshidalinezhadian@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 23:55:00 +0330
Subject: [PATCH] camera: include BufferQueue.h for the HALv1 flash control

CameraHardwareInterfaceFlashControl::initializePreviewWindow() creates
a BufferQueue for the torch preview surface. On LineageOS 22.2
(Android 15) no header CameraFlashlight.cpp includes brings in
<gui/BufferQueue.h> any more, so libcameraservice failed to compile:

  CameraFlashlight.cpp:554:5: error: use of undeclared identifier
  'BufferQueue'

Include it directly.

Change-Id: I2f7c9a4e1b6d3f8a0c5e2b9d7a4f1c6e8b3d0a57
---
 services/camera/libcameraservice/CameraFlashlight.cpp | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/camera/libcameraservice/CameraFlashlight.cpp b/services/camera/libcameraservice/CameraFlashlight.cpp
index 4ece1f0..868a08a 100644
--- a/services/camera/libcameraservice/CameraFlashlight.cpp
+++ b/services/camera/libcameraservice/CameraFlashlight.cpp
@@ -21,6 +21,9 @@
 #include <utils/Log.h>
 #include <utils/Trace.h>
 #include <cutils/properties.h>
+// The HALv1 flash control creates its own BufferQueue for the preview window. On
+// Android 15 none of the headers below pull BufferQueue.h in any more.
+#include <gui/BufferQueue.h>
 
 #include "CameraFlashlight.h"
 #include "camera/CameraMetadata.h"
-- 
2.43.0

